  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Recommended for anyone on 5.7.4: that version could silently hide real concurrency bugs, because LC046 stopped reporting named-set operations whose name came from a parameter or field. LC046 now reports them again, and separately no longer produces false positives outside loops for operations whose required arguments provably make them fault before starting, such as null or blank raw SQL, a null key array, or a cancelled token.",
